    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0820" n="810" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pilcher</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-01-22T10:00:00-05:00">January 22, 1948—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>119. Dept would appreciate receiving more precise information, including verbatim
                    text if available, of reported (urtel 121, Jan 19<anchor n="3" xml:id="d700-f1"
                    />) Red warning to missionaries and other foreigners in central China who
                    assisted allied forces during war to get out of China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
